    "extracted text": "The study investigates A356 aluminum alloy with trace additions of Ni or V at nominal concentrations of 600 ppm and 1000 ppm respectively. Specimens were tested in both sand cast and permanent mould cast conditions, in both as-cast and T6 heat treated states. The T6 heat treatment included solutionising at 540°C for 4 h followed by quenching in a water bath at 20°C, and subsequent aging at 160°C for 6 h. The cooling rate for sand cast samples was approximately 1.3 K/s, while for permanent mould cast specimens it was 4.2 K/s.",
